  <h3>1. Key Orders (Silsilas) in India</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Chishti Order:</strong> Founded in India by **Khwaja Moinuddin Chishti** (established dargah at Ajmer, visited by Akbar). 
      <br/>- *Beliefs:* Highly liberal, integrated local yogic practices, stayed away from royal politics.
      <br/>- *Saints:* Baba Farid (verses included in Guru Granth Sahib), Hazrat Nizamuddin Auliya (Delhi, called Mehboob-i-Ilahi), Sheikh Salim Chishti.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Suhrawardi Order:</strong> Founded by Shihabuddin Suhrawardi. Active in Punjab/Sindh. Accepted state offices, wealthy order.</li>
    <li><strong>Naqshbandi Order:</strong> Founded by Khwaja Bahauddin Naqshbandi. Most orthodox and conservative order. Opposed music and liberal policies of Akbar. Supported by Aurangzeb.</li>
  </ul>
`;

